  "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nI would like the Download Client widget to display the 50 latest added downloads. To do this, I `Enable items sorting` and set it to sort by `Added` with `Invert sorting` enabled, however, this fails to show the latest added downloads, and instead shows a random selection of 50 downloads (the number set in `Limit items per integration`).\n\nWhile the random selection of downloads are indeed sorted by their `Added` value, the widget is rendered kind of useless in this use case, as it's not displaying the true latest 50 added downloads, but instead grabbing 50 random downloads and then sorting them by `Added`.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Add Download Client widget\n2. Configure the widget as follows:\n\n<img width=\"624\" height=\"831\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/639b3f32-f57f-4065-b922-95e6eeafad05\" />\n\n3. Save & exit editing mode (as the sorting doesn't seem to work while in edit mode)\n4. Observe the random selection of 50 downloads, instead of 50 latest downloads\n5. Optional - adjust the items limit up/down to see some newer downloads appear/disappear from the widget.\n\n### Impact\n\nIf you want to use the Download Client widget to see the latest completed/incomplete downloads, unfortunately this is not possible unless you are willing to increase the items limit value to above your total number of downloads (not feasible if thousands).\n\n### Additional information\n\nThis behaviour/bug was not present pre 1.0, and worked as expected before migrating. I migrated today and I am using Homarr v 1.40\n\n### Version\n\nOther (describe in \"additional information\")\n\n### Installation method\n\nUnraid Apps\n\n### Browser\n\nChrome",
