      "body": "So it turns out that setting the `Limit items per integration` to a number above my total torrent count (3500+) results in a completely unresponsive server within a couple of hours, requiring a forced reboot. Upon further inspection, I noticed `kernel: Out of memory: Killed process 654818 (qbittorrent-nox)` in my unraid syslog every ~2 hours.. qbittorrent (v5.1.2) was steadily consuming all 32GB of my systems memory with steady uniform CPU spikes every ~5 seconds. For reference, my qBit usually only uses around 500mb of memory. Stopping the Homarr docker container or changing the items per integration value back to 50 immediately and permanently fixes the issue (until upping the limit value again). ",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
